{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Boolean bus",
  "exampleId": "block-boolean-bus",
  "description": "Two Boolean pulse trains, the gate commands of a half bridge, are bundled by a Boolean Bus Creator into one bus named by signal (high, low) and carried across the sheet on a single heavy Boolean wire. The Bus Selector picks low by name and the NOT inverts it; AND checks that both gates are never on together, so it stays false. A bus carries one kind of signal: set the type under Signals before wiring a bus block, or wire it and it takes the kind of the first wire. Results shows a Boolean bus element by element as 0 or 1.",
